  <p>What does this table tell us? First, that the obvious rules don’t work very well. Only the two rules that lower the tier save anything at all, and the better one captures 24 % of the oracle’s saving while failing in 9 of the 43 sessions on tasks the user’s own choice completed. Lowering effort alone saves too little per task to pay for the redos. Second, “always use the top cell” barely changes anything, simply because most users already do it. The distance between these rules and the oracle is the room a learned router has to work with.</p>
